WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.825
Click Saturn.

00:00:00.825 --> 00:00:01.966
Look at the rings.

00:00:01.966 --> 00:00:03.742
Now think about the numbers.

00:00:03.742 --> 00:00:08.373
Saturn itself is about one hundred and twenty thousand kilometers across.

00:00:08.373 --> 00:00:15.160
The main ring system stretches another two hundred and eighty thousand kilometers beyond the planet's edge.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.586
And those rings are, in places, only ten meters thick.

00:00:18.586 --> 00:00:19.283
Ten meters.

00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:20.615
A two-story building.

00:00:20.615 --> 00:00:27.403
A disc the diameter of nearly the distance from the Earth to the Moon, and it's the depth of a small house.

00:00:27.403 --> 00:00:28.925
The rings are not solid.

00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:35.839
They are billions of pieces of water ice, most of them centimeter-sized, some meter-sized, a few house-sized.

00:00:35.839 --> 00:00:38.440
Each piece is on its own Keplerian orbit.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.246
Pieces near the inner edge orbit Saturn in about five hours.

00:00:42.246 --> 00:00:44.846
Pieces near the outer edge take fourteen.

00:00:44.846 --> 00:00:46.622
And then there are the gaps.

00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:57.850
The Cassini Division — three thousand kilometers of nearly empty space between the A ring and the B ring — was carved by the gravity of Mimas, one of Saturn's small inner moons.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.387
Mimas is fifty thousand kilometers away.

00:01:00.387 --> 00:01:10.409
And yet, by orbital resonance — its two-to-one gravitational pull on any particle that tries to settle in that band — it has swept the Cassini Division clear.

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:19.987
In September 2017, the Cassini spacecraft — having spent thirteen years in orbit around Saturn — was deliberately plunged into the planet's atmosphere.

00:01:19.987 --> 00:01:30.200
Its final twenty-two orbits, called the Grand Finale, took it weaving between the planet and the inner edge of the rings, photographing them from inside the gap.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:35.084
Those photographs are what you see when you look at the rings on this screen.

00:01:35.084 --> 00:01:38.129
Two hundred and eighty thousand kilometers wide.

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:39.207
Ten meters thick.

00:01:39.207 --> 00:01:41.808
Read that again and let the ratio settle.

